      "mandate": "fix-issue-10-in-pkravella-mandate-sandbox-title",
      "task": "Fix issue #10 in pkravella/mandate-sandbox.\n\nTitle: taskId collides for two tasks that start with the same words\n\n`taskId` in src/ids.js returns `slug(text)`, and `slug` truncates at 48 characters on a word boundary. Two different tasks whose opening words match therefore get the same id, and anything keyed on it silently overwrites.\n\n`node --test test/ids.test.js` fails on \"distinguishes two long tasks that start with the same words\".\n\nExpected: `taskId` is stable for the same input and distinct for different inputs, while staying readable — appending a short digest of the full text is the usual fix. `slug` itself should keep its current behaviour, because other callers rely on it being a plain slug.\n\nRepository: pkravella/mandate-sandbox. Read a file before updating it, because an update needs its sha. Work on a branch named agent/slug-collides-on-truncation and open a pull request when you are done, unless the issue says otherwise. When you are finished, say DONE.",
